## VIVA QUESTIONS AND ANSWERS

### Q1. What is DevOps?
DevOps combines development and operations to improve software development, deployment, and maintenance.

### Q2. What is MLOps?
MLOps applies DevOps practices to machine learning development, deployment, monitoring, and updating.

### Q3. What is CI?
Continuous Integration automatically builds and tests code changes.

### Q4. What is CD?
Continuous Delivery or Continuous Deployment automates the process of preparing or deploying software updates.

### Q5. What is Continuous Training?
Continuous Training automatically retrains machine learning models using new data when required.

### Q6. Why is CI/CD important in machine learning?
It helps automate testing and deployment, making model updates faster and more reliable.

### Q7. What is Git?
Git is a version control system used to track code changes.

### Q8. What is automated testing?
Automated testing checks code and model behavior without requiring manual testing each time.

### Q9. What is model monitoring?
Model monitoring checks the performance and behavior of a deployed machine learning model.

### Q10. What is data drift?
Data drift occurs when real-world input data changes compared with the data used to train the model.

### Q11. Name some DevOps tools.
Git, GitHub, Jenkins, Docker, and Kubernetes.

### Q12. What is the main benefit of MLOps?
It makes machine learning systems easier to build, deploy, monitor, and update reliably.

